cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or its results, please cite the article (preferred-citation) and this repository."
type: software
title: "ATO1-Marche-Nord-forecasting: code and reference outputs for honestly-benchmarked forecasting of civil water demand and network losses (ATO1 Marche Nord, Italy, 2017-2021)"
abstract: "Leakage-free, rolling-origin, five-seed benchmarking of deep-learning (LSTM, Transformer, CNN-LSTM, MLP), gradient-boosted-tree, SARIMA and naive forecasts of monthly civil water demand and network losses in ATO1 Marche Nord (Italy), 2017-2021, across three feature specifications. Includes the three pipelines (Jupyter notebooks), cached public covariates, per-seed and aggregated metric tables, and the figure script. Operator data are withheld (available on request)."
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-08"
license: MIT
